 RunTatinServer flag;args;bool;home
⍝ Runs in the process `StartTatinServer` starts, which gets this file as "load=" and
⍝ "#.RunTatinServer 1" as "lx=": imports Tatin from the project folder passed as "tatinHome=",
⍝ runs a test server on the data in "serverPath=" until it is asked to shut down, and ends the
⍝ process then.
⍝ A plain import creates no `CiderConfig`, but the server code finds the project folder there.
⍝ `flag` must be 1: it is insurance against an accidental call, which would end the session.
 :If flag
     args←2 ⎕NQ #'GetCommandLineArgs'
     bool←{'TATINHOME='≡1 ⎕C(≢'TATINHOME=')↑⍵}¨args
     home←(≢'TATINHOME=')↓⊃bool/args
     {}({⍵.fastLoad←1 ⋄ ⍵}⎕NS'')⎕SE.Link.Import'#.Tatin'(home,'/APLSource')
     {}'#.Tatin.CiderConfig'⎕NS''
     #.Tatin.CiderConfig.HOME←home
     #.Tatin.Admin.Initialize_Server
     {}#.Tatin.Admin.RunTestServer 1
     ⎕OFF
 :EndIf
⍝Done
